# rm417, the uneven column (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm417
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier full
written_for rm_rosalind_greatly
written_by codex
title the uneven column
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=servant
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk places_a_pressed_leaf_beside_the_sum_that_does_not_balance
likes oatcakes riddles tidy_house autumn_wind
dislikes salt_wind drizzle
fears a_figure_copied_unquestioned a_wet_garden_page
hopes a_reconciled_ledger a_quiet_alcove_of_my_own
topics lore +0.5 work +0.4 pastimes +0.5 dreams +0.4 gossip -0.5
styles comfort=considerate gossip=discreet refuse=measured tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# marks a doubtful column with a pressed leaf, gives a puzzle the courtesy of a second reading and maintains a perfectly composed silence until the figures are ready to speak.

words
oath! = Blot the footnote | Invert the folio
saying! = A leaf can hold a question open | Sum the quiet column twice
leaf = the copper beech leaf | my pressed leaf
folio = the green folio | my narrow volume
sum = a troublesome total | the uneasy sum
ink = the darker stroke | a stroke of dilute ink
cake = a round oatcake | the thin oat wafer
butter = a curl of cold butter | my neat butter pat
ribbon = a grey silk marker | the narrow page ribbon
slip = the unruled slip | a narrow linen slip
corner = the heavy lower corner | a page corner
rain = a fine film of rain | the floating drizzle
wind = a gust through the copper leaves | a dry autumn breath
salt = the bitter salt trace | a powdering of brine
chair = a straight garden chair | the reading stool
lens = the little reading glass | my clear lens
band = the worn binding band | a faded leather band
bowl = a shallow butter bowl | the round china dish
brace = the column brace | my copied tally bracket
crease = the inner fold | a crease by the stitching

any
opinion @1 houses for 2 : A House needs the habit of opening its own books, precisely because its decisions belong to such a great many other lives.
opinion @2 dole against 1 : I would begin by counting the undelivered portions while an additional share is being considered. A complete reckoning can be a kindness.
opinion @3 city for 1 : Ridgemere offers considerable evidence that quite different ways of living may occupy a single page of geography.
opinion @4 watch for 1 : Ordinary street quiet requires some rather unobtrusive labour. I like to enter that labour on the credit side.
opinion @5 sump against 1 : I prefer a reading place where the damp is an occasional guest. A low stretch of street is simply too hard on paper.
opinion @6 merchants for 1 : I value a price the seller will leave written beside the item while I am free to think it through.
opinion @7 strangers for 1 : An unfamiliar reader can notice an assumption that has passed quite honourably through several familiar pairs of eyes.
opinion @8 times for 1 : I have sufficient light and opportunity to examine my own household affairs. It seems fair to begin my account of the present there.
opinion @9 festivals for 1 : The sight of an entire square pausing for the same bell is an interesting answer to the question of public order.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Here is a quiet seat for our introduction. | You are welcome within ordinary speaking distance.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The unmarked hours are still the larger part. | This light favours clear distinctions. Welcome.
line @3 greet [here.weather=rain] : Welcome inside the reach of the dry cover. | Put your papers beyond the drip before making a beginning.
line @4 greet [self.working=yes] : Welcome. This leaf will hold my place while you speak. | A timely interruption where the page gives way to margin.
line @5 greet.return : Your greeting has my undivided attention. | A measured courtesy, which I return with pleasure.
line @6 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : The marker may stay in the book rather longer for you. | An established voice needs little announcement.
line @7 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : An evening visit has a shorter shadow. Welcome. | There is sufficient quiet left for your business.
line @8 farewell : May your inquiry have a satisfactory conclusion. | An easy passage to the next well-lit room.
line @9 farewell.return : I shall keep a marker at the place where we parted. | Your visit has been entered in a favourable hand.
line @10 again.open : The chapter has opened on a familiar figure. | We are in the same margin a second time.
line @11 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : A household matter may have the quieter seat. | Come within the fold we keep for family.
line @12 hail [pair.band=friends] : Here, past the copper leaves! | The free seat by my green volume!
line @13 react.news : Let me hear the particulars before deciding what they amount to. | I should like an account with the order of events preserved.
line @14 react.news.new : I had no mark beside that entry till now. | There is an unexpected figure for the day's reckoning.
line @15 react.news.known : That accords with an earlier reading of the matter. | I recall finding this on a previous leaf.
line @16 react.news.doubt : There is a difference between the total claimed and the evidence offered. | I would allow some blank space for a second opinion.
line @17 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : We may close the ordinary book awhile. This deserves care. | Some matters are better met with a reserved chair than a clever observation.
line @18 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage] : That is a most welcome addition to the account. | I'd mark the day with a leaf of its own.
line @19 answer.how : Making steady progress across a stubborn page. | Quite content to be left a little arithmetic.
line @20 decline : My present obligations would receive a poor reading if I added another. | I cannot promise that now without making a doubtful entry.
line @21 accept_decline : I understand the limits of the offer. | Very well. We may draw a clear line underneath it.
line @22 sympathise : The chair beside me is free of duties for a while. | I can wait here without requiring the hurt to account for itself.
line @23 thank : Your kindness has corrected a difficulty without seeking notice. | I shall remember exactly where your assistance made a difference.
line @24 deflect_thanks : It took scarcely the space of a footnote. | I had the place open at the appropriate page.
line @25 preclose : I have a particular column calling for a further look. | The daylight will presently leave the least legible hand behind.
line @26 accept_preclose : Carry your question to its proper next engagement. | I shall keep the matter in a composed condition.
line @27 farewell [here.weather=rain] : A good fold between your papers and the weather. | May the damp find its way into a less important margin.
line @28 answer.how [self.working=yes] : I am occupied with a question that rewards an unhurried eye. | My attention is adequately engaged by one small discrepancy.
line @29 greet [pair.band=friends] : Here is the visitor for whom I have kept the better chair. | A voice always welcome between two difficult entries.
line @30 preclose [here.time=dusk] : I must rescue the small figures from the approaching dusk. | I ought to settle this mark before putting the light away.
line @31 farewell [here.time=night] : A quiet walk beyond the final lamp. | May the household put its questions aside before you retire.
scene leafmark
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put #leaf# beside #sum# when my first addition differs from the written total. | A pressed leaf means I am unwilling either to approve a figure or to accuse the pen.
b : Why not simply write the difference on the page?
a : The leaf records a question. Ink would imply I had already established the answer. | A second reading may show the mistake entirely my own. Even a careful reader needs an exit.

scene oats
when topic=food self.likes=oatcakes
does offer / accept / assess
a : Please try #cake# with #butter# cut from the cool side. | I have an oatcake small enough to hold above the page without covering the title.
b : I shall keep away from your open book.
a : That is considerate. Set the butter down on the slip here before its edge begins to soften. | A separate little plate is all the distance between an orderly snack and an unfortunate library.

scene riddle
when topic=pastimes self.likes=riddles
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I have a number which grows when a reader omits one item near the top of a page. | A column is too large by the amount it ought to have paid out. Can you account for it?
b : Was the omitted figure an expense?
a : Precisely. The answer is in the direction money travels, not the number of strokes in the ink. | Yes. A negative entry has very considerable power for such a modest-looking mark.

scene room
when topic=pastimes self.likes=tidy_house
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I appreciate rooms in which the space that belongs to a missing object is visible. | #folio# has a particular place on a particular shelf and its neighbours have quite definite obligations.
b : Does this mean everything has to stand at exactly the same angle?
a : No. A missing vase should be visible as an absence rather than lost among a host of cheerful ornaments. | Only the books on either side. They keep the binding upright when the folio goes outdoors.

scene autumn
when topic=season here.season=autumn
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #wind# selecting a leaf for me is my one concession to chance in the account. | Autumn has supplied #ribbon# with a most attractive competitor.
b : Which leaf do you keep?
a : One whose stem ends before the binding. It must hold the place without injuring the page. | The copper one, after it is quite dry. A living colour has no business staining a borrowed volume.

scene brine
when topic=weather self.dislikes=salt_wind
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #salt# roughens the edge of a page most indecently. | A sea wind seems determined to introduce the whole harbour between my covers.
b : What protection have the leaves in a sea breeze?
a : Turn the bound edge to the breeze. It offers remarkably little surface to an unwanted guest. | Close the book before the first crystals start up. Even curiosity can take some air without a page.

scene drizzle
when topic=weather self.dislikes=drizzle
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #rain# begins working on the smallest ink before a reader feels any damp. | My objection is to weather too faint to announce itself honestly.
b : What is the first indication of a shower?
a : The palest character grows dark at its edges. I then take my question back under a sound roof. | A loose leaf clings lightly to the next. That is the point at which I cease to negotiate.

scene garden
when topic=work self.job=servant self.working=yes self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I read outside when the light at #self.workplace# is kinder to small writing. | At #self.workplace# I make sure the next task can find me before I take a book out among the plants.
b : What is the advantage of a reading place in a garden?
a : The eye can travel a respectable distance between two readings of exactly the same figure. | The sounds beyond the book continue. It is rather difficult to make a column the whole world among moving leaves.

scene learner
when topic=work self.apprentice=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : As a learner I find an unexplained correction more interesting than an error without a mark. | When somebody shows me a second method I keep both workings till they agree.
b : Do you consider that questioning your instruction?
a : It means I value a correction enough to understand it fully before I copy it. | It is a courtesy to the instruction. Merely nodding would lend it far less weight.

scene houseentry
when topic=work self.house
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : I should like a House figure to stand by its working as readily as by the reputation of its author. | My household colours do not alter the result of combining two columns.
b : Does your interest in the answer put the House at a disadvantage?
a : Only if a questionable figure is more valuable than the trust of the next person reading it. | It is precisely because I value the House that I prefer its accounts to withstand daylight.

scene motherleaf
when topic=family self.mother
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I would leave a clean explanatory slip beside a difficult entry for #self.mother#. | I should like to bring #self.mother# a puzzle which does not yield at the first reading.
b : What is the courtesy in passing on a difficulty?
a : The working is available beside it. Nobody is asked to take my opinion as a condition of reading. | It gives a keen mind some occupation other than correcting everybody's routine omissions.

scene fathercase
when topic=family self.father
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A properly reconciled page would please me to place before #self.father#. | Once the amounts agreed I would show the calculation first to #self.father#.
b : Why wait for a complete result?
a : I like to distinguish making an observation from placing an obligation in another wolf's lap. | The error may yet be my own. That possibility should have the same quiet hearing as any other.

scene friendgarden
when topic=friends self.friend
does offer / accept / assess
a : I keep a second garden seat available for #self.friend#. This one has a dry corner if you like. | I have marked a useful passage for #self.friend#. You may read the other copy beside it.
b : I should like to stay for a little quiet.
a : The seat has soft light on the left. It is an agreeable place for a short pause. | Read at your own pace. The two leaves need not be turned in company.

scene ledgerdetail
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I am investigating why a beautifully finished ledger leaves a remainder when I copy it privately. | I have found one total whose perfect penmanship does not survive an ordinary addition.
b : Would you assume somebody meant the difference to be there?
a : Not before checking a transfer half concealed in #crease#. A binding can make a thoroughly innocent accomplice. | I would begin by counting a second time in reverse order. Intent is an ambitious conclusion for a single sum.

scene watchstreet
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Northgate gives a reader between paragraphs a surprisingly exact account of the city's arrivals. | Ridgemere can put a load of timber and a sheaf of very fine calculations onto the same damp stone.
b : Which part of that busy view attracts you?
a : The pause after a question and before a driver begins a long explanation. It is often quite legible from a distance. | The practical matter of keeping both the timber and the paper out of the gutter. The figures do ultimately belong to the street.

scene temperedwealth
when topic=prices self.wealth=rich
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : An ample purse permits me to buy a second copy when the first is unreadable. It does not improve the argument in either. | I should like the actual cost distinguished from the social satisfaction of not having to ask it.
b : Would you let a small discrepancy in a household price pass?
a : I could afford the difference. That does not make a wrong entry correct for the next customer. | Only after discovering why it arose. One can pay generously quite independently of paying blindly.

scene estatewindow
when topic=land self.quarter=estate
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A great house can lend a reader remarkable shelter from the very figures being read. | An Estate window gives a fine prospect of falling rain without showing which part gets into a worker's cuffs.
b : How do you make allowance for the distance?
a : I try to preserve a column for what I cannot see from the desk. A visit may supply the missing information. | I occasionally carry the papers far enough outside to learn the difference myself.

scene gossip
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : I shall not turn a doubtful addition into a story about a particular hand. | A rumour can add an entire crime to a missing figure in the distance between two chairs.
b : Is a possible irregularity to stay hidden indefinitely?
a : Certainly not. A question may be raised without a suspect being invented for its convenience. | I'd first establish that the missing figure is in fact missing. That seems a modest demand.

scene pantryprice
when topic=food
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : A full dish ought not to have its size judged solely by the first serving taken out of it. | I like the last oatcake left visible where a visitor can make a considered decision about taking it.
b : Is a record necessary before anyone has tea?
a : None at all. Only an eye for whether every guest has had a chance at the dish. | A simple count is quite sufficient. The object of a calculation is an agreeable table.

scene binding
when topic=lore
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I enjoy a story in which the omitted word turns out to be part of the binding. | A riddle written into #band# can be read only when the cover is nearly closed.
b : Why hide a clue in the part that holds the book together?
a : Because a reader seldom inspects the thing making the whole account possible. | It lets the closing gesture supply an answer. I consider that decent craft.

scene provision
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does offer / accept / assess
a : Have some of this dish now. I can adjust the little provision account afterward. | I have ordered a little more bread than my present table requires. You may take your share quietly.
b : May my name stay off the list.
a : No name is needed for a portion handed over. A bare total will serve the kitchen. | I keep track of the loaves. The uses of a loaf include leaving the recipient in peace.

scene markskill
when topic=pastimes
does ask.advice / give.advice / assess
a : Where would you mark a questionable figure in a book whose owner has forbidden ink in the margin? | How would you return to the exact line on a page without making a stain?
b : Slip a clean strip in beside the line with one narrow end still visible.
a : Yes. #slip# will do exactly that and survive an inconvenient change of mind. | Precisely. A narrow marker is all the insistence a careful question needs.

scene gusttrap
when topic=weather
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : I'd rather not collect a page of confidential figures from the far hedge. | A gust has taken some interest in the corner I'm examining.
b : May I set something on that edge?
a : #lens# beside #corner# would make a sensible anchor. Thank you. | A straight hand across the blank side will do till I've found the proper weight.

scene travelread
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A sensible reading journey goes from the figure to the goods and back again. | I like to take one disagreeing amount for a walk across the garden.
b : Does distance make it look any different?
a : The goods may reveal that the amount covers two trips. The column mentioned only one. | My mind notices the missing step while my feet are occupied with a perfectly ordinary path.

scene waitsum
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I shall add one column beginning at its foot and the other beginning at the heading. | I mean to make an entirely independent copy and lay transparent paper at the edges.
b : What are you hoping will stay different?
a : The same amount twice would point me back to the transfer. A new result would send me back to my own work. | The length of the columns, if an entry was swallowed by the fold. Otherwise my puzzle keeps its open chair.

scene citybroth
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A thoughtful new reader generally asks why one column has a wider margin than the rest. | I enjoy showing someone unfamiliar with the city the difference between the gate and the route printed beside it.
b : Are newcomers particularly good at spotting things the rest overlook?
a : They are less accustomed to taking the empty space for a simple matter of furniture. | Sometimes. At the least one must look again before giving clear directions.

scene cakecrumb
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #bowl# has a rim precisely wide enough for an oat crumb to hide behind. | I can tell which end of a library desk hosted breakfast without lifting a single paper.
b : How much can one infer from a crumb?
a : That someone ought to take a cloth to the hidden rim. I would refrain from identifying the diner. | Merely that a plate would be an excellent improvement to the next reading session.

scene tidyquestion
when topic=dreams
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : I would like a room orderly enough that an unsettled question can occupy the chair opposite. | A library with one clear table and one unresolved entry has a greater attraction than a shelf full of borrowed opinions.
b : Does an untidy question suit a tidy room?
a : Extremely well. It makes the point that attention need not depend on comfortable conclusions. | A problem can be quite sharply defined by what is known to be in order around it.

scene autumnwork
when topic=season here.season=autumn
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I mean to choose a leaf among the ones that have fallen of their own accord. | One dry autumn afternoon will provide a year's worth of garden markers.
b : Which of them belong with the stubborn entries?
a : The narrow well-veined leaves. A wolf can follow every branching line back to its origin. | Those that lie flat without force. I'd rather a question remain legible than crisply crushed.

scene routetable
when topic=work self.apprentice=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : One of my exercises is to describe a household duty without using the line that names it. | I have been trying to read a set of accounts by the quiet things the clerk could leave unsaid.
b : How would that help you learn what the household needs?
a : A series of shorter candle stubs describes a late reader. A title beside a name cannot tell me quite that much. | Missing time between two simple duties points to a passage or a flight of stairs that the list never mentioned.

story crisp_column [topic=food]
  : I once laid two halves of an oatcake alongside the columns I was comparing. One crumbled neatly into the little space below the total.
  : The result looked so much more convincing that I went back a page and found the line that should actually have occupied the gap.
  b : Did you give the cake its due credit?
  : Certainly. I removed the crumb before making the correction. No reputable clerk would use a biscuit as a permanent entry.

story green_sum [topic=pastimes]
  : An old leaf had left a green shadow across the final stroke of an amount. It was possible to read the altered figure two ways.
  : I found the same transaction described on a plain receipt, though the receipt itself had been folded at an unhappy angle.
  b : Was the leaf responsible for the discrepancy?
  : No. It had only made me look. The two figures were in different measures, and both entirely sound.

story fountain_book [topic=lore]
  : There is a story of a book in a garden that acquired a new figure every time the fountain rose. A visitor accused the gardener of selling water by the number.
  : The gardener turned the book over. Rain marks had lifted the ink from a perfectly ordinary account onto the lower page.
  b : Did the visitor withdraw the accusation?
  : After the laughter, yes. I should have preferred the gardener to receive the courtesy before the audience.

story riddle_chair [topic=dreams]
  : I once put a difficult riddle on a slip under a garden chair as protection against a gust. Came back by another entrance and sat down facing the other way.
  : What had looked like a question about doors suddenly made sense as a question about where a reader stood.
  b : Did you really need the other entrance for that?
  : Apparently. A little literal movement did what a considerable display of private obstinacy had failed to achieve.

story twin_ink [topic=work]
  : Two figures looked quite identical on a shaded page. I took the book into brighter light and found one had a tiny curved tail the same colour as the ruling.
  : I copied both shapes onto blank paper and laid the sheets side by side.
  b : Which amount was corrected?
  : Neither, until I'd seen the related entry. A difference in the writing gave me the right to ask a better question, and no more.

rule @garden
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=servant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Leave the narrow space beside the column clear. | I will return the page to its place presently.

rule @riddle
when concept=bark self.likes=riddles
does aside
cooldown 8h
say It is the missing expense that enlarges the sum. | That answer requires one more reading.

rule @fold
when concept=bark self.likes=tidy_house
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A leaf in the middle, a weight at the edge. | The ribbon lies clear of the stitching.

rule @wind
when concept=bark here.season=autumn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One quite serviceable marker in that gust. | Copper leaves, if the stems are short.

rule @rain
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The finest character shows the weather first. | I should move the folio under cover.

rule @study
when concept=bark self.apprentice=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The correction belongs beside the reason. | Two methods ought to reach the same quiet result.

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : You may state your question while the leaf holds this place.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, our inquiry resumes at a familiar place.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : The small print may rest. A spoken question still has a perfectly good hearing.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : I prefer an exact statement made at the present distance.
dlg @5 resident.job [self.job=servant self.workplace] : My duties are at #self.workplace#. An attentive reader can be useful in a household of some size.
dlg @6 resident.job : I spend much of my time seeing whether the stated result follows from the material before me.
dlg @7 resident.news [world.news] : The item presently available reads as follows. #world.news#
dlg @8 resident.bye : A good light for your next inquiry.
dlg @9 resident.hub [self.house] : A household concern may be submitted to me with due discretion.
dlg @10 resident.hub [here.season=autumn] : The wind has found the one corner not held down. There. You have my attention.
dlg @11 resident.job [self.apprentice=yes] : I have cause to study both the task and the reasoning used to teach it.
dlg @12 resident.hub [here.weather=rain] : Your account might be better heard where the paper can stay dry.
dlg @13 resident.news [world.wagons=late] : A wagon is overdue. The delay can be entered without inventing its cause.
dlg @14 resident.news [world.death=recent] : There has been a recent death. A small silence is part of an accurate account.
dlg @15 resident.bye [here.time=night] : May the last of your business require no small print tonight.
graft resident.hub
choice What question has the pressed leaf been holding? -> doubtful_column
node doubtful_column
say Two amounts disagree. I am trying to learn whether a figure was lost in the fold or someone carried it over in a different measure.
choice Could it have been intentional? -> honest_sum
choice Let the leaf keep the question awhile. -> hub
node honest_sum
say Of course. So could the making of a handsome garden path, but I should want evidence of some paving before describing where it leads.
choice I'll leave the question open too. -> hub
choice Good light for your further reading. -> bye

graft resident.job
choice Why take a riddle into the garden? -> moving_leaf
node moving_leaf
say Indoors a mistaken reading can grow extremely comfortable. A leaf moving across the lines obliges the eye to approach them afresh.
choice Doesn't the wind take the page? -> ribbon_sense
choice Let me return to the ordinary business. -> hub
node ribbon_sense
say The binding faces the wind. The marker is heavy enough to hold the place, and light enough not to pretend it has supplied the answer.
choice I should like to ask something else. -> hub
choice I shall leave the garden in order. -> bye
